<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.20.xsd">

    <!--
        Rotate the platform SuperAdmin credential (audit blocker B1 / D-03).

        WHAT IS WRONG WITH 900. Changeset 900-001 seeds superadmin@restaurantos.io and states its
        plaintext password in a comment three lines above the hash. Anyone who has ever cloned this
        repository — or read it on a mirror, a CI log or a fork — holds the credential for the
        highest-privilege account in the system. Until plan 13-05 that account could not actually
        log in anywhere, which is the only reason this was not already an incident; the moment a
        platform login exists, it is one.

        WHY THE NEW ROW RECORDS NO PLAINTEXT, NOT EVEN IN A COMMENT. The practice being retired here
        is exactly "the hash is in the changeset and the password is in the comment next to it". The
        credential for this project's SuperAdmin is documented in
        .planning/phases/13-platform-tenant-access-repair/13-CONTEXT.md and in the phase seed script,
        and BOTH of those — along with this hash — must be rotated before any production deployment.
        A deployment that ships this file unrotated ships a known password.

        WHY THE OLD ROW IS DEACTIVATED AND NOT DELETED.
          * impersonation_log.admin_user_id references platform_users(id); deleting the row would
            either fail on the constraint or orphan the audit trail of everything that account did.
          * A deactivated row is visible evidence that the rotation happened. A missing row is
            indistinguishable from a database that never had the seed applied.
        PlatformAuthService refuses an inactive user through the same generic 401 as an unknown
        email, so is_active = false is a real revocation, not a cosmetic flag — and 13-05's live
        script asserts that the retired credential now returns 401 through the real gateway.

        WHY THE ID IS DETERMINISTIC. uuid5 over the namespace scripts/onboarding.py uses
        (6ba7b810-9dad-11d1-80b4-00c04fd430c8) with the name
        "restaurantos/platform/user/superadmin@softxlogic.com", giving
        eca6bbf2-ce62-5d16-8f4c-d052521d16ad. Plan 13-15's seed script can then reference the
        account without a lookup, and re-provisioning a database reproduces the same id — so an
        impersonation_log row written against one environment still resolves in another.

        Both changesets are guarded by their own sqlCheck precondition with onFail="MARK_RAN",
        matching the idiom in 900, so a second run is a no-op rather than a unique-violation.
        Context: seed — same as 900/901, so a production changelog run without the seed context
        applies neither the old seed nor this rotation.
    -->

    <changeSet id="platform-910-001-seed-project-super-admin" author="restaurantos-agent" context="seed">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">
                SELECT COUNT(*) FROM platform_users WHERE email = 'superadmin@softxlogic.com'
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <insert tableName="platform_users">
            <column name="id" value="eca6bbf2-ce62-5d16-8f4c-d052521d16ad"/>
            <column name="email" value="superadmin@softxlogic.com"/>
            <!-- BCrypt cost 12. The plaintext is deliberately not recorded here; see the header. -->
            <column name="password_hash" value="$2b$12$4aU1pMaZTR4stNbyBZEHr.Yj8W1m694L2QyYfLF841JLTO9vNVWwW"/>
            <column name="role" value="SUPER_ADMIN"/>
            <column name="is_active" valueBoolean="true"/>
        </insert>
        <rollback>
            <delete tableName="platform_users">
                <where>email = 'superadmin@softxlogic.com'</where>
            </delete>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="platform-910-002-deactivate-seeded-super-admin" author="restaurantos-agent" context="seed">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="1">
                SELECT COUNT(*) FROM platform_users
                WHERE email = 'superadmin@restaurantos.io' AND is_active = true
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <update tableName="platform_users">
            <column name="is_active" valueBoolean="false"/>
            <where>email = 'superadmin@restaurantos.io'</where>
        </update>
        <rollback>
            <update tableName="platform_users">
                <column name="is_active" valueBoolean="true"/>
                <where>email = 'superadmin@restaurantos.io'</where>
            </update>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
